.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341240" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{3}+x"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}-x"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-x"] ["math" "|-{x}^{3}+x|"] ["math" "|x{|}^{3}+|x|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341240" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{3}+x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=(2x+1){e}^{2x}$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is the value of $f(-2)?$\n\n$f(-2)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the even extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =F(-x) \\\\  & =(2(-x)+1){e}^{2(-x)} \\\\  & =(-2x+1){e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =(-2(-2)+1){e}^{-2(-2)}=5{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5e^4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-2x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **even** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the even extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =F(-x) \\\\  & =(-x)^{2}-2(-x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{2}+2x"] ["math" "-{x}^{2}-2x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+2x"] ["math" "|-{x}^{2}+2x|"] ["math" "|x{|}^{2}+2|x|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[{x}^{3}+2x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }({\\pi }^{3}+2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =2({\\pi }^{2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340814" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-340814" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340814" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi^2+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{3}{2}-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340815" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-340815" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-340815" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{\\pi}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(4\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\sqrt{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341283" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341283" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{\\pi}(\\sqrt{2}-2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(6\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{6(\\sqrt{3}-2)}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341285" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341285" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341285" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{\\pi}(\\sqrt{3}-2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=5{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3}+2x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =2(\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341276" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341276" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10\\pi^2}{3}+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=-2x+5$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(5-\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-2x+5$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2x+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-2x+5\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[(-2x+5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{2}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-2\\pi +5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{2}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(0-\\frac{2}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi ))}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(5-\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{2(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341269" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=10x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{n}.$$\\,{a}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}\nfor $n\\ge 1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=10x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{20}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{20}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{20(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-1)}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{20((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{20(1+(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{10((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{20((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{20((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{20(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341259" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{20((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=5x+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(2+\\frac{5}{2}\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=5x+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x+2\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[(5x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{5}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((5\\pi +2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{5}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{5}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{10(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-1)}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{10((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(2+\\frac{5}{2}\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aad8f09049d423367798d634c28a5568a9b65da839c2ae5f564abbf9c448150b"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{\\pi n}"] ["math" "\\frac{5(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{10((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341265" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(1+\\frac{3}{2}\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x+1\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[(3x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{3}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((3\\pi +1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{3}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{3}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-1)}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{6((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(1+\\frac{3}{2}\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068558/state.json" "file_sha256" "a8ef3971ca071ae0b4af2a88138fe25a2bbd413fee03d78a5f880160968cf41e"} {"question" "q-341267" "field" nil "attribute" "